{"id":"la-rioja","name":"Chilecito, La Rioja","country":"Argentina","story":"Sparse, episodic mountain and scrub fires: a low-count region where sensor changes dominate raw trends.","places":["La Rioja","Chilecito","Famatina"],"lang":["es"],"bbox":[-68.6,-30.0,-66.6,-28.2],"grid_deg":0.1,"data_through":"2026-11-10","built_at":"2026-11-10T16:40:16+00:00","estimand":{"primary":"Hotspots per period on the Aqua MODIS scale: the number of vegetation-fire detections Aqua MODIS would have recorded (early-afternoon and post-midnight passes). Day and night are calibrated separately and added.","why_aqua":"The early-afternoon orbit is the only one observed continuously from 2002 (Aqua) through Suomi-NPP, NOAA-20 and NOAA-21. Converting VIIRS to MODIS scale discards information and is well-posed; the reverse must invent small fires MODIS never saw, so the VIIRS-scale view is marked modelled before 2012.","secondary":["Fire cell-days (0.1° cell × UTC day with ≥1 detection), Aqua scale","Hotspots on the Suomi-NPP VIIRS scale (modelled before 2012)","Persistent heat sources (kilns, flares, industry, volcanoes) harmonized separately","Raw detections — not comparable across satellite eras"],"not":"Not burned area and not a count of fires: a detection is one hot pixel in one overpass."},"method":{"confidence_filter":"drop VIIRS 'l' and MODIS confidence < 30 (no crosswalk between the two scales); sensitivity reported","static_mask":"0.01° cells where science-quality FIRMS `type` is 1–3 for ≥50% of ≥3 detections","coverage":"share of days each satellite delivered data anywhere on Earth in each period (measured, so launches, gaps and the Suomi-NPP end come from the data); below 25% a satellite is left out, otherwise counts are divided by coverage","calibration":"ratio of totals per calendar month, day and night separately, shrunk toward the pooled ratio by empirical Bayes (shrinkage strength estimated from the data). Chain: Terra→Aqua (2002–2020, bridges 2000–2002 only), Suomi-NPP→Aqua (2012–2020, pre-drift), NOAA-20→Suomi-NPP, NOAA-21→NOAA-20; chain-closure mismatch is added to the error","combination":"inverse-variance mean of the satellites observing each period (calibration error + counting noise, evaluated at the pooled mean); intervals widened so 95% of held-out months fall inside (MODIS-denial test)","comparison":"each period vs the same month/week in other complete years: median, ratio, percentile, rank — no sigma thresholds (fire counts are skewed)","weekly":"ISO-8601 weeks; weeks use their Thursday's month calibration","provisional":"periods containing near-real-time rows are provisional: FIRMS replaces NRT with standard processing after ~3 months, and the mirror keeps only one of the two, so the NRT-to-standard difference cannot be measured from it"},"calibration":{"veg_det_D":[{"sensor":"MODIS_T","reference":"MODIS_A","window":["2002-08","2020-12"],"beta":[0.6778,0.4944,0.4515,0.6062,0.8652,1.1824,0.9812,1.0489,1.0373,1.4034,0.8453,0.7197],"pooled":1.0072,"sigma2":0.3285,"tau2":0.238,"n_periods":218,"calibrated":true},{"sensor":"VIIRS_SNPP","reference":"MODIS_A","window":["2012-02","2020-12"],"beta":[0.1934,0.1165,0.12,0.1547,0.1692,0.2193,0.1827,0.2005,0.1404,0.1613,0.1712,0.1243],"pooled":0.1647,"sigma2":0.0047,"tau2":0.1406,"n_periods":107,"calibrated":true},{"sensor":"VIIRS_NOAA20","reference":"VIIRS_SNPP","window":["2018-05","2026-10"],"beta":[1.0284,1.1144,0.9984,0.9361,1.036,1.0295,0.8993,1.0967,1.1088,1.3218,1.1237,0.8575],"pooled":1.0674,"sigma2":0.044,"tau2":0.02,"n_periods":97,"calibrated":true},{"sensor":"VIIRS_NOAA21","reference":"VIIRS_NOAA20","window":["2024-02","2026-10"],"beta":[0.6172,0.6657,1.9562,0.8161,0.9096,1.0748,1.3187,0.9387,0.9884,0.7191,0.8833,0.5834],"pooled":0.936,"sigma2":0.0025,"tau2":0.2514,"n_periods":31,"calibrated":true}],"veg_det_N":[{"sensor":"MODIS_T","reference":"MODIS_A","window":["2002-08","2020-12"],"beta":[0.8922,0.8133,0.8948,0.8655,0.8655,0.9751,0.7565,0.9617,0.8961,0.8393,0.8313,0.8162],"